00:23:22.520 --> 00:23:27.560
For BluffBench 1, we did run it telling the model to ignore the labels. And that

00:23:27.560 --> 00:23:32.359
does improve performance because the labels are part of the expectations about

00:23:32.359 --> 00:23:36.280
what the plot is going to be. If you're plotting a known data set, and then you

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:43.800
have the X and Y axis labeled in a way that matches the well-known data set, that

00:23:43.800 --> 00:23:51.880
feeds into the model's priors. So, we did run the BluffBench 2 against GPT 5.6.

00:23:51.959 --> 00:23:57.000
So, I think performance on the first BluffBench would almost certainly improve

00:23:57.000 --> 00:24:02.839
if we stripped those, stripped those out. The issue is that, like, you probably

00:24:02.839 --> 00:24:06.920
don't want to do this for your agent. We don't want to do this in Posit Assistant

00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:10.839
because we want to hand the agent the actual plot object without doing any sort

00:24:10.839 --> 00:24:15.239
of manipulation behind the scene, which is probably what you want to, like, you

00:24:15.239 --> 00:24:18.760
want the model to be able to look at a reasonable plot without having to do

00:24:18.760 --> 00:24:21.400
weird things to manipulate it and be accurate.

